{#
  Renders a page's Sources declaration from its `sources` frontmatter.

  The frontmatter is the single declaration: `verify:provenance` gates it, and this partial publishes
  it, so the table a reader sees and the record a refresh sweep reads cannot drift apart. Pages that
  restate nothing declare `sources: original` and render no table.

  It renders as a footer rather than as a `## Sources` heading. As a heading it was the last section
  of nearly every page, which made a table of links into other repositories read as the payoff of
  the page rather than as its provenance (KI-WEBSITE-SITE-024). The declaration is unchanged and still
  complete; only its weight on the page is.

  See docs/guides/developer/page-provenance.md.
#}
{% if sources and sources != 'original' %}
<footer class="prose-provenance">
  <p class="overline">Written from</p>
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr><th>Source</th><th>Governs</th><th>Last reviewed</th></tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
    {%- for source in sources %}
      <tr>
        {%- if source.url %}
        <td><a href="{{ source.url }}">{{ source.title or source.url }}</a></td>
        {%- else %}
        <td><a href="https://github.com/{{ source.repository }}/blob/{{ source.ref }}/{{ source.path | replace(" ", "%20") }}">{{ source.title or (source.repository + "/" + source.path) }}</a> at <code>{{ source.ref }}</code></td>
        {%- endif %}
        <td>{{ source.governs }}</td>
        <td>{{ source.reviewed }}</td>
      </tr>
    {%- endfor %}
    </tbody>
  </table>
</footer>
{% endif %}
